      { "b", 1, "Added the Stat Calculator: a panel beside the character window with every stat in one Character Stats section, where each number comes from, what the next point buys, the Stat Weights pane, a gear comparison and the Ability Scaling tab. Turn it on in Bonus Features > Stat Calculator. It is off until you do." },
      { "b", 1, "Opens with the character window when you left it open, from the Stat Calculator row in the XayaUI minimap button's list, or with /xui stats. Opened on its own, Esc closes it." },
      { "b", 1, "The panel and its minimap row are hidden in combat and come back after combat." },
      { "b", 1, "Stat Calculator settings saved by an earlier test version are kept." },
      { "dev", 2, "Developers' notes: Not yet tested in game (docs/plans/STAT-CALCULATOR-MAIN-INGAME-CHECKS.md). There is no Stat Calc button on the character window: that button belongs to Improved Character Display, which is not part of this download." },
    } },
    { date = "2026-11-09", title = "Rules Only", blocks = {
      { "h3", "Rules 0.7.0" },
      { "grp", "Install (read this first)" },
      { "b", 1, "Delete the XayaUI_Rules_Options folder from Interface\\AddOns. The rule editor is now part of XayaUI Rules, so that folder is no longer used." },
      { "b", 1, "XayaUI Bonus Features, XayaUI Chat, XayaUI Dev Assist and XayaUI QoL are no longer part of this download for now. Switch them off in the game's AddOns list or delete their folders: an old copy left on would run against the new XayaUI." },
      { "b", 1, "Keep your XayaUI_Media folder if you put your own pictures or sounds in it. XayaUI still reads it." },
      { "grp", "Rule editor" },
      { "b", 1, "The rule editor is now part of XayaUI Rules. It works as before and is still built only the first time the settings window opens." },
      { "dev", 2, "Developers' notes: Not yet tested in game. Its code is now read at login with XayaUI Rules: about 1.4 MB of memory, measured in standard Lua 5.1, not in the game client." },
      { "h3", "Options 0.6.107" },
      { "grp", "Settings window" },
      { "b", 1, "The settings window now sets up the rule editor from XayaUI Rules instead of loading a separate addon." },
    } },
    { date = "2026-11-08", title = "Gradient Borders", blocks = {
      { "h3", "XayaUI 0.6.81" },
      { "grp", "Themes" },
      { "b", 1, "Added gradient borders to the cursor trail themes: the settings window's frame, panes, buttons and tabs are drawn with a border that runs through the trail's colors. Solid themes draw exactly as before." },
      { "b", 1, "Added a \"Reverse gradient direction\" switch on the Theme page, under the theme choice. It is independent of the cursor trail's own Reverse, and is saved and shared with the theme." },
      { "b", 1, "Added \"Use the gradient as the color of\" in Advanced customization, which lets the gradient be the color of any palette color. Six earlier theme strings still import unchanged." },
      { "dev", 2, "Developers' notes: Not yet tested in game (QA B294 to B296; walkthrough \"debug-w9\"). Issue #460. Chosen for you, change it in the Questions flow: a box's gradient runs left to right and a line along its length; only the settings window and core's flat buttons get gradient borders (not the version pane, the import window, the Blizzard Reskin, Character or Chat windows, dropdown boxes or the Esc menu button); anything else that asks for one solid color still gets the old color; and there is one Reverse per theme." },
      { "h3", "Options 0.6.102" },
      { "grp", "Theme" },
      { "b", 1, "The Theme page carries the new switch and the gradient color list." },
    } },
    { date = "2026-11-08", title = "Debug Batch W7", blocks = {
      { "h3", "Options 0.6.100" },
      { "grp", "Settings Window" },
      { "b", 1, "Clicking an option in the rule editor now does about half the work it did: the width of dropdown text is measured once and cached (by font, size, flags and scale) instead of on every click. In the test stand-in, game calls per click went from 53,802 to 27,704." },
      { "dev", 2, "Developers' notes: Measured in the test stand-in only, not in game; the real click time needs your re-run of the J31 walkthrough (\"perf-settings-click\") and the new \"debug-w7\" walkthrough (QA B293). Issue #467 stays open." },
    } },
    { date = "Older notes", title = "Older patch notes", blocks = {
      { "p", "Older patch notes are not kept in the game, so the settings window stays light. All patch notes are in PATCH-NOTES.md at https://github.com/heyitsxaya/XayaUI." },
    } },
  },
  readme = {
    { "h2", "What XayaUI is" },
    { "p", "XayaUI is a group of addons. Each one is its own entry in the game's AddOns list (under XayaUI), so you can switch any of them off; the game needs a /reload after a change there." },
    { "b", 1, "**XayaUI** (XayaUI Platform in the AddOns list) holds saved settings, themes, sharing, profiles, the Recycle Bin, sound and media lists, XayaUI's error record, the minimap button and the Esc-menu button. Every other XayaUI addon needs it." },
    { "b", 1, "**XayaUI Rules** holds the rules (cooldown, aura and other triggers), cues, conditions and actions, combat aura tracking, rule sharing and backups. Switch it off if you make no rules." },
    { "b", 1, "**XayaUI Options** is the settings window, with everything that only works while it is open: the rule editor, the mover, Combat Tracking Setup, the talent scan and the displays' right-click menu. The game reads it the first time you open the window, so it costs nothing until then." },
    { "b", 1, "**XayaUI Debug** holds the debug tools: the console window, the bug report, the debug report, `/xui status`, `/xui auras` and `/xuiengine`. The game reads it only while Settings > Debugging > **Advanced Debugging** is on (off by default), once per login or /reload." },
    { "b", 1, "**XayaUI Bonus Features** holds the Stat Calculator's switch (Bonus Features > Stat Calculator, or `/xui stats`) and the Calculator (Bonus Features > Calculator, or `/xui calc`). The Stat Calculator itself is the separate entry XayaUI Bonus Features: Stat Calculator, which the game reads only the first time you open it, and never while it is off." },
    { "p", "A feature you switch off costs nothing: it runs no timers, listens to no events and keeps no frames. Your settings are kept either way. (The minimap button and the Esc-menu button are part of XayaUI itself; switched off, they are not built.)" },
    { "h2", "Getting started" },
    { "b", 1, "Open the settings window with `/xui`, the XayaUI minimap button, or the XayaUI button in the Esc menu." },
    { "b", 1, "**Rules** is where you make and edit rules. A rule watches something (a trigger), and when it is true it plays cues (a sound, speech, an icon), checks conditions and runs actions." },
    { "b", 1, "**Bonus Features** lists the Calculator and the Stat Calculator in the left pane. The tick box beside each name turns it on or off at once; no reload is needed." },
    { "b", 1, "**Settings** (the toolbar button) holds UI Options (Display, Rule Creation, Theme), the Minimap Button and Debugging." },
    { "b", 1, "Click the version text in the settings window's bottom-left corner for this window: Patch Notes and Info. The **?** in the title bar opens Help." },
    { "h2", "Features at a glance" },
    { "b", 1, "**Auto-Generate Rules.** Builds a first batch of rules for your spec: one skeleton rule per cooldown, and you choose which to make. Rules > Auto-Generate Rules." },
    { "b", 1, "**Combat Tracking Setup.** Sets up buff durations for your class and spec. The very first time you open the settings window it opens with it; after that, use **Open Combat Tracking Setup** on the Rules tab. It closes with the settings window." },
    { "b", 1, "**Stat Calculator.** A panel beside the character window with your stats, gear and ability scaling. Bonus Features > Stat Calculator, or `/xui stats`. It loads the first time you open it. It closes when a fight starts and stays closed until you open it again." },
    { "b", 1, "**Calculator.** A small calculator window, and sums in chat: `/xui calc 23,249 / 3,472`. Bonus Features > Calculator (on unless you switch it off)." },
    { "b", 1, "**Themes.** Colors and fonts for every XayaUI window. Settings > UI Options > Theme." },
    { "b", 1, "**Debugging.** Advanced Debugging (off by default) loads the debug tools at the next login or /reload and shows XayaUI's own Lua errors with its messages. XayaUI saves its own errors and warnings either way (never its ordinary messages); `/xui bug` lists them. While it is on, every login and /reload prints one chat line saying so. Settings > Debugging." },
    { "h2", "Slash commands" },
    { "b", 1, "`/xui` opens or closes the settings window (`/xayaui` works too)." },
    { "b", 1, "`/xui help` lists every command you can use." },
    { "b", 1, "`/xui unlock` opens the settings window with the mover on, so you can drag displays and groups. The mover works only while the settings window is open: closing the window closes it. Moves you have not saved are kept, and the next time you open the window one question asks you to save them, discard them or keep editing." },
    { "b", 1, "`/xui disable` turns every rule off at once, in combat too; `/xui enable` turns them back on (after combat, if you are in a fight). A /reload also turns them back on." },
    { "b", 1, "`/xui stats` opens the Stat Calculator, while it is on (with XayaUI Bonus Features). If it cannot load, it says why each time you type it." },
    { "b", 1, "`/xui calc` opens the Calculator; `/xui calc` and a sum answers in chat. `/calc` works too, unless another addon uses it." },
    { "b", 1, "A command of a part that is switched off prints one line saying where to turn it on, for example \"XayaUI: The Calculator is off. Turn it on in /xui > Bonus Features.\"" },
    { "b", 1, "`/xui debug` lists the diagnostic commands." },
    { "p", "These are debug tools: they need Advanced Debugging on and a /reload. With it off, each answers with one chat line saying so." },
    { "b", 1, "`/xui console` opens the XayaUI console: its messages, and a line to type commands in." },
    { "b", 1, "`/xui status` prints every rule's answer right now, and why." },
    { "b", 1, "`/xui auras` prints aura IDs, and whether XayaUI can follow them in combat." },
    { "b", 1, "`/xui bug` makes a bug report, with XayaUI's saved errors and warnings." },
    { "b", 1, "`/xuiengine` shows what the combat engine draws." },
    { "b", 1, "`/xui debug perf on`, `/xui debug perf` and `/xui debug perf off` measure the combat engine: how often it re-checks, its CPU and memory." },
    { "p", "In combat the settings window, the rule editor and the mover do not open: one chat line says so, and the one you asked for opens by itself when combat ends. A window that is open when combat starts closes and opens again afterwards." },
    { "p", "The full manual is docs/USER-GUIDE.md in the XayaUI source code (Info > Version info has the link)." },
  },
  faq = {
    { "h2", "Rules not firing" },
    { "h3", "My rule never fires." },
    { "p", "Usually one of its inputs is unknown (shown in yellow), or the rule does not load. Type `/xui status` (or `/xui debug status`) for every rule's answer right now and why, read the Right now lines, and check the dots on the condition rows. `/xui status` is one of the debug tools: turn on **Advanced Debugging** (Settings > Debugging) and type `/reload` first." },
    { "h3", "The rule fires but I get no sound or display." },
    { "p", "The rule has conditions, but no cue is listed in any enabled condition's THEN row. Open the rule's Conditions tab and add the cue there." },
    { "h3", "The rule does not load at all." },
    { "p", "Its group is set to Never, a group's class, spec, role or instance setting keeps it out, or a talent requirement is not met. The Load tab's banner says \"Overridden by group...\" when a group is the reason." },
    { "h3", "It works out of combat but not in combat." },
    { "p", "The value it reads is secret in combat, so the answer becomes unknown. The Right now line shows it; see \"What the game won't allow\" below." },
    { "h3", "It fires one or two seconds early." },
    { "p", "Spell Usable ignores the cooldown. Use \"Usable AND off cooldown\" instead." },
    { "h3", "It says \"not set: cooldown state\" or \"a trigger (none added yet)\"." },
    { "p", "A section is in use but its State dropdown is blank, or there is no trigger and both states are blank. Fix it on the Trigger tab." },
    { "h2", "Auras and the Cooldown Manager" },
    { "h3", "How do I find an aura's ID?" },
    { "p", "Turn on **Advanced Debugging** (Settings > Debugging) and type `/reload` once: `/xui auras` is one of the debug tools. Then, out of combat, with the aura on you (a training dummy works), type `/xui auras` for your buffs or `/xui auras debuffs`. `/xui auras <spell ID or name>` prints the same facts for one spell and works anywhere, in combat too." },
    { "h3", "Can XayaUI follow this aura in combat?" },
    { "p", "The same command answers it:" },
    { "b", 1, "**Readable in combat:** \"yes (never secret)\" for the few auras the game always lets addons read; otherwise \"no (secret in combat, encounters, Mythic+ and PvP)\"." },
    { "b", 1, "**Cooldown Manager:** \"on and shown\" means XayaUI sees the aura in combat. \"Offered ... but not switched on\" means your spec's Blizzard Cooldown Manager has it: turn it on there (Tracked Buffs or Tracked Bars)." },
    { "h3", "Why can't XayaUI add the aura to the Cooldown Manager for me?" },
    { "p", "Blizzard keeps that window closed to addons. When a rule needs it, the rule's Display and Cues tabs say where to add it." },
    { "h3", "Why is my group's border drawn around each icon, not around the whole group?" },
    { "p", "A group's **Border** and **Background** (group page > Group tab > Border and background on each display) are drawn on each display in the group, one by one, in every group, including the icons the combat engine draws in combat. **Padding around each display** sets how far they reach past each display's edge; it starts at 0, right on the edge. Groups inside the group use them too, unless they turn on their own." },
    { "h3", "Can I switch the combat engine off?" },
    { "p", "No. The combat engine (it draws your aura displays through the game's own aura frames, so time and stacks show in combat) runs whenever any rule is on, and it has no switch of its own. To stop it, turn every rule off with `/xui disable` (until `/xui enable` or a /reload), or switch XayaUI Rules off in the AddOns list. A rule you switch off has no display, so the engine draws nothing for it. Nothing else stops it: there is no speed guard any more (older versions could draw only your current spec's displays, or stop drawing until a /reload, when the game's CPU meter read high). An \"engine off\" setting saved by an older version is no longer used; it is cleared the first time this version loads, and one chat line says so. `/xuiengine` shows what the engine draws; it changes nothing (it is one of the debug tools, so it needs Advanced Debugging)." },
    { "h3", "The Combat Tracking Setup window: where is it, and why did it stop opening by itself?" },
    { "p", "It sets up buff durations for the class and spec you are playing (it scans your spells and talents and learns real durations from your own casts out of combat). It no longer opens over the game by itself after login or a spec change. The very first time you open the settings window, if no spec has a setup yet, it opens together with it. After that, open it with the **Open Combat Tracking Setup** button on the Rules tab (or on Settings > UI Options > Rule Creation). It closes when you close the settings window, and it cannot open in combat. Its step 2 (Learn) records your casts only while it is open, so keep the settings window open while you cast your self-buffs (out of combat)." },
    { "h3", "My \"Only when not mounted\" sound played while I was still mounted." },
    { "p", "That can happen in a fight, on purpose. With **Let the game play this sound on the aura itself** ticked, the game's copy of an **Only when not mounted** sound is set up as each fight starts, even while you are mounted, because the game does not let XayaUI set it up during the fight. That way, if you are knocked off your mount in the fight, the sound still plays. In that fight it may also play while you are still mounted. When the fight ends and you are mounted, the copy is taken back." },
    { "h3", "The sound pane says \"XayaUI plays this sound itself\"." },
    { "p", "The rule has **Let the game play this sound on the aura itself** ticked, and its buff has an icon in your Cooldown Manager. Then XayaUI plays the sound itself instead of handing a copy to the game, because it can see that icon in a fight and so can follow every setting of the rule (Load tab, triggers, conditions, Repeat). Two small differences: if the buff is already up (or already gone) when a fight starts, a rule that loads only in combat plays once as the fight starts; a buff lost and gained again in the same instant makes no sound." },
    { "h3", "The sound pane says \"The game would not take this sound when a fight started\"." },
    { "p", "The game refused the rule's copy at the start of a fight (or at a boss pull). For the rest of the session XayaUI keeps the copy from before the fight, so the sound still plays, but it may also play when your Load tab says no. To make it exact, add that buff to Blizzard's Cooldown Manager: then XayaUI plays the sound itself and follows every setting." },
    { "h3", "Why doesn't the game's copy of my sound repeat?" },
    { "p", "The game plays its copy on the aura alone, so it can never repeat it (**Repeat**) or wait for the rule's other triggers, conditions or ANY trigger mode. Everything on the Load tab is followed. If you need Repeat, add the buff to your Cooldown Manager (XayaUI then plays it itself, with Repeat, in fights too), or untick **Let the game play this sound** (XayaUI's own sound repeats, but in a fight it plays only for auras XayaUI can see)." },
    { "h2", "What the game won't allow" },
    { "h3", "Why is there no trigger for health, mana, rage or the combat log?" },
    { "p", "In Midnight (12.x) primary resources, combat log events, health, other units' casts and creature identity are not available to addons, so those triggers were not ported. Enemy aura reads are unavailable too." },
    { "h3", "Why do some answers go unknown in combat?" },
    { "p", "Buff and debuff reads in restricted content may be secret. The Cooldown Manager icon is the fallback, and only for spells tracked there. Target Debuff in combat relies on the spell being tracked in the Cooldown Manager buff viewer." },
    { "h3", "Why does my glow action do nothing?" },
    { "p", "A glow needs the LibCustomGlow library, which XayaUI does not ship. Enable ElvUI, BigWigs or another addon that ships it." },
    { "h3", "Why don't my custom cues play?" },
    { "p", "Custom cues can be made but do not yet play, show or run anything." },
    { "h3", "Why can't my chat action send to other players?" },
    { "p", "The game restricts chat actions to other players in several kinds of content, and combat numbers cannot be put in chat." },
    { "h2", "Commands and reporting" },
    { "h3", "Where are the commands?" },
    { "p", "`/xui help` lists the commands you can use right now: a part's commands are listed only while that part is on. The diagnostic ones are under `/xui debug`; `/xui debug` alone lists them. The debug tools (the console window, `/xui bug`, `/xui report`, `/xui status`, `/xui auras`, `/xuiengine`, and `/xui debug status`, `perf` and `auras`) work only while **Advanced Debugging** is on (Settings > Debugging, off by default; type `/reload` after turning it on). Until then each says so in one chat line. With them on, any `/xui debug` command opens the XayaUI console and prints there." },
    { "h3", "Why does /xui stats (or /xui calc) say it is off?" },
    { "p", "Each part's commands work only while that part is switched on. Typed while it is off, they run nothing and print one line naming the part and where to turn it on, for example \"XayaUI: The Calculator is off. Turn it on in /xui > Bonus Features.\" Tick the part's box in the settings window (**Bonus Features > Stat Calculator** or **Bonus Features > Calculator**); it works at once, with no reload. There is no `/xui stats on` any more." },
    { "h3", "/xui stats keeps saying the Stat Calculator could not load." },
    { "p", "It says why every time you try: it is switched off in the game's AddOns list, its folder is missing, or its files stopped with a Lua error. Fix that, then type `/reload`. After a Lua error, nothing of it starts, and the error is saved for the bug report (see \"Does XayaUI save its error messages?\" below). If another addon takes over the game's Lua error handling, the Lua error itself may not be saved." },
    { "h3", "The Stat Calculator closed when a fight started and did not come back." },
    { "p", "That is on purpose: it never stays open in a fight and does not reopen by itself afterwards. Open it again from the **Stat Calculator** row in the minimap button's list, with `/xui stats`, or by opening the character window again. It also loads only the first time you open it, not at login." },
    { "h3", "Does /calc work?" },
    { "p", "Yes, while the Calculator is on: `/calc 12k*3` answers in chat, and `/calc` alone opens or closes the Calculator window. If another addon already uses `/calc`, XayaUI leaves it to that addon; `/xui calc` always works." },
    { "h3", "Why does /xui unlock open the settings window?" },
    { "p", "The mover (dragging your displays and groups on screen) is part of the settings window and works only while it is open. `/xui unlock` opens the window with every display unlocked; closing the window closes the mover. Moves you have not saved are kept. The next time you open the window, one question asks: **Save**, **Discard** (everything goes back) or **Keep editing** (the mover opens with them). Nothing is asked at login. If combat closed the window, the mover opens again by itself with your moves when combat ends." },
    { "h3", "Why does chat say \"Advanced Debugging is on\" every time I log in?" },
    { "p", "Because Advanced Debugging is on (Settings > Debugging). While it is on, every login and /reload prints \"XayaUI: Advanced Debugging is on. Turn it off in /xui > Settings > Debugging.\", so you always know the debug tools are loaded. To stop it, untick Advanced Debugging and type `/reload`." },
    { "h3", "How do I see how much work the combat engine does?" },
    { "p", "Turn on **Advanced Debugging** and type `/reload`. Type `/xui debug perf on`, play a fight, then `/xui debug perf` for the report and `/xui debug perf off` to stop. It counts each kind of re-check and the redraws, shows the most in one second (as a range such as \"10 to 14\" when it cannot be pinned down; at exactly 10 a second it can read \"possibly over\"), and the game's CPU meter and memory for each XayaUI addon. For your CPU limits, read the game's AddOn Usage screen." },
    { "h3", "Why won't the settings window open in combat?" },
    { "p", "The settings window, the rule editor, the mover (`/xui unlock`), Combat Tracking Setup, the talent scan and `/xui enable` are locked in combat, because rules and combat tracking are changed only there. Ask in combat and one chat line says so, for example \"the settings window can't open during combat. It will open when combat ends.\": it then opens by itself when combat ends (only your last request is kept)." },
    { "b", 1, "**Open when combat starts:** the window closes (unsaved rule edits go to Rule Drafts) and opens again where you were when combat ends. The mover closes and opens again with your unsaved moves." },
    { "b", 1, "**Still allowed in combat:** `/xui disable`, closing any window, `/xui report`, `/xui bug`, `/xui console`, `/xui help`, `/xui status`, `/xui auras`, `/xuiengine` and the `/xui debug` commands that only read, such as `/xui debug talents status`." },
    { "h3", "How do I turn every rule off at once?" },
    { "p", "Type `/xui disable`. It works in combat too: every rule stops checking, and their displays, glows and sounds stop (a sound already playing finishes). They stay off until you type `/xui enable` or `/reload`. `/xui enable` waits until combat ends if you are in a fight; rules then start fresh, as after a /reload." },
    { "h3", "Where are XayaUI's messages?" },
    { "p", "In the main chat window, the XayaUI console window (`/xui console`), or both: choose under Settings > Debugging, \"XayaUI's messages\". The console window is one of the debug tools: while they are not loaded (Advanced Debugging was off at your last login or /reload), every message goes to the chat window. If you turn Advanced Debugging off during play, the tools stay loaded and your choice still applies until the next /reload." },
    { "h3", "Does XayaUI save its error messages?" },
    { "p", "Yes. Every error or warning XayaUI prints in chat is also saved, with a code, whether or not Advanced Debugging is on. Ordinary messages are not saved. To see them, turn on Advanced Debugging (Settings > Debugging), type `/reload`, then type `/xui bug`." },
    { "h3", "How do I report a problem?" },
    { "b", 1, "Turn on **Advanced Debugging** (Settings > Debugging; recommended, off by default), then type `/reload`. It loads the bug report and the debug report. XayaUI saves its own errors and warnings by itself whether or not it is on, so you do not have to remember a command, and errors from before you turned it on are kept too." },
    { "b", 1, "Type `/reload` (or log out): the game writes its files only then." },
    { "b", 1, "Send `XayaUI.lua` from `World of Warcraft\\_retail_\\WTF\\Account\\<your account folder>\\SavedVariables\\`. Settings > Debugging shows the exact path and what to send." },
    { "b", 1, "`/xui bug` makes a bug report; `/xui report` shows XayaUI's errors with their codes, ready for a screenshot." },
    { "h3", "My backups show 0 rules after I went back to an older XayaUI." },
    { "p", "Backups are now kept as compact text, which older XayaUI versions cannot read. Loading one there changes nothing. Return to this version and they are all there again." },
  },
}
